  "ChangeLog": [
    {
      "Version": "1.6.10",
      "Date": "2026-11-09",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Documentation cleanup and content pruning. Strikethrough the apache 2.4 claim in the manual-checklist note (readme lines 26-28) since q4 2026 scap content covers it (shipped in v1.6.9); inline amendment added. Prune ws2012 r2 scap benchmarks from StigContent\\ since those products are no longer in the deployed baseline. iis 8.5 server/site benchmarks kept since iis 8.5 is still in rotation. No WS2016/WS2019 scap content in StigContent\\ yet -- flag for a follow-up pass."
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.6.9",
      "Date": "2026-11-09",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Build-Package.ps1 now actually copies SCAP\\ and StigContent\\ into the deployment zip. The v1.3.0 changelog claimed scc and scap benchmark content shipped in the zip but the build script never had copy logic for either folder, so every release from 1.3.0 to 1.6.8 shipped without them -- targets had no way to run scc scans without a separate manual drop. Also drops the redundant inner scc-5.12_Windows.zip from staging (duplicates what SCC_5.12_Windows_Setup.exe already installs) to keep the zip size reasonable. StigContent\\ ships whatever disa scap benchmark zips sit in the repo folder at build time; curate per product set before building. StigContent\\ has also been refreshed with q4 2026 scap benchmarks for apache server and apache tomcat -- these products had been manual-checklist-only in prior releases, so this is new automated scan coverage."
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.6.8",
      "Date": "2026-07-27",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Enable TCP/IP NetBIOS Helper (lmhosts). Prior baseline disabled lmhosts (Start=4) which broke NBT short name resolution on non-domain WS2019: net use \\\\SHORTNAME\\share returned 'network path not found' even with the share up and firewall open. Flipped disablenetbioshelper -> enablenetbioshelper (Start=2, Automatic) in all three OS configs so LCM autocorrect keeps it running. Bootstrap.ps1 also gets a new step 1a that enables and starts the service immediately, so the fix takes effect before the first LCM pass."
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.6.7",
      "Date": "2026-07-23",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Skip V-213958 (clr enabled) on SQL 2017 config only. SqlServerConfiguration was reasserting sp_configure 'clr enabled', 0 every 15 min via LCM autocorrect — surfaced as intermittent CLR outages to the app owner. SqlServer2016STIG.ps1 left strict pending a 2016 instance requiring the same. Active skip rules reference section in readme.txt updated to match."
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.6.6",
      "Date": "2026-07-06",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Fix WS2022 skip list — V-254276 removed from skip. Post-review found V-254276 is the SMBv1 disable rule (SMB1=0), not FIPS as previously labeled; skipping it disabled a security control we want on. WS2022 STIG has no dedicated FIPS rule so the disablefips registry resource is now documented as drift protection only. Also added a landmine/known-behavior section to readme.txt covering SQL audit ON_FAILURE=SHUTDOWN, SqlScriptQuery destructiveness, and the bootstrap port 1433 assumption for cyber/ops awareness."
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.6.5",
      "Date": "2026-06-30",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Add full skip rule parity to WS2022 (V-254439/435/281/459/276/458), matching 2016/2019 environment exemptions. Add OrgSettings DOS banner body (V-254457), DOS caption registry resource, and disablefips registry block to WS2022. Add active skip rules reference section to readme.txt above changelog for cyber review."
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.6.4",
      "Date": "2026-06-30",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Skip SA disable rules (V-214028 sql2016/2017, V-274444 sql2022) and add Force=$true to disablefips and disablenetbioshelper across all OS configs. V-214028/V-274444 SetScript runs ALTER LOGIN [sa] DISABLE on principal_id=1 — disabled the install admin account on awis-sql2-SOW making it appear removed. disablefips and disablenetbioshelper were missing Force=$true causing WS2019 LCM consistency check to fail every 15 min when those pre-existing registry values needed overwriting."
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.6.3",
      "Date": "2026-06-30",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Fix named instance connection: remove port from named instance ServerInstance string. PowerSTIG splits on backslash so localhost\\INST1,PORT put the port inside instanceName, breaking SqlProtocol WMI lookup. Named instances now use localhost\\INSTANCE (shared memory for local connections). Default instance keeps localhost,1433 (port in server name is safe -- no backslash so SMO reads it correctly)."
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.6.2",
      "Date": "2026-06-24",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Fix sql named-pipe deployment failure: bootstrap now passes localhost,PORT (default instance) or localhost\\INSTANCE,PORT (named) to force tcp. Skip tls 1.0 SCHANNEL rules (V-213967.a/.e/.i/.m for sql 2016/2017, V-271310.b for sql 2022) that were breaking ssis packages."
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.6.1",
      "Date": "2026-06-17",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "apply.ps1: LCM Disabled-mode check at startup + try/catch around post-apply Test-DscConfiguration so a transitional LCM state doesn't crash an already-completed apply run"
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.6.0",
      "Date": "2026-06-17",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Oracle 12c/19c removed from configmap — DISA manual checklist only, no PowerSTIG/DSC automation available. Detection kept for logging; replaced misleading warn with explicit info message."
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.5.9",
      "Date": "2026-06-17",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Fix SQL named instance: detect instance name from Instance Names\\SQL registry values instead of hardcoding MSSQLSERVER; also fixes false SQL2012/SQL2014 detections from client tools"
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.5.8",
      "Date": "2026-06-10",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Fix Oracle not detected when ORACLE_HOME_VERSION is absent — falls back to parsing major version from KEY_ subkey name (e.g. KEY_OraDB19Home1 -> 19)"
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.5.7",
      "Date": "2026-06-03",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Fix oracle detection crash under strict mode — ORACLE_HOME_VERSION property access now guarded via PSObject.Properties before dereference"
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.5.6",
      "Date": "2026-06-02",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Explicitly disable FIPS via registry on 2016 (V-225059) and 2019 (V-205842) — rules are skipped in PowerSTIG but EnabledFips=0 now enforced to prevent accidental drift"
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.5.5",
      "Date": "2026-05-21",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "2019 STIG skip rules and banner config translated from 2016 baseline"
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.5.4",
      "Date": "2026-05-20",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Build-Package fixes: all configs included in zip, VMware modules excluded, archive naming collision fixed"
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.2.0",
      "Date": "2026-04-11",
      "Author": "Ryan",
      "Notes": "Bump STIG version to 2.10 and PowerSTIG to 4.29.0 to match vendored module"
    },
    {
      "Version": "1.1.0",
